  <h2>Classic DQ Cake vs. Blizzard Cake — Which Should You Order?</h2>
  <p>The classic DQ Cake uses standard vanilla and chocolate soft serve with the signature hot fudge and crunch center. It is the DQ cake that most people grew up with and is the safest choice for mixed-preference groups.</p>
  <p>Blizzard Cakes cost $3–$5.75 more for the same size but include actual Blizzard mix-in pieces throughout the soft serve layer. The Oreo Blizzard Cake — at $38.74+ — is the most popular DQ Cake overall, beating the classic version in orders. If you know your group loves Oreo, Cookie Dough, Reese's, or Choco Brownie, the Blizzard Cake upgrade is clearly worth it.</p>

  <h2>How to Order a DQ Cake — Step-by-Step</h2>
  <ol style="padding-left:1.4rem;line-height:2;">
    <li><strong>Call or visit your local DQ at least 48 hours before your event.</strong> More notice is better during peak seasons (June–July, December).</li>
    <li><strong>Choose your size</strong> based on guest count: 8-inch (8–10), 10-inch (12–16), Sheet Cake (24–32).</li>
    <li><strong>Choose your flavor</strong>: Classic DQ, Oreo Blizzard, Cookie Dough Blizzard, Reese's Blizzard, or Choco Brownie Extreme.</li>
    <li><strong>Add your personalized message</strong> — included free with all custom cakes.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask about decoration options</strong> — color customization and photo toppers at select locations.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick up with a cooler</strong> — DQ Cakes are large and need to stay frozen during transport.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>DQ Cake Ordering Tips from Regular Customers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order larger than you think you need.</strong> DQ Cake portions tend to be generous, but running out of cake at a party is worse than having leftovers.</li>
    <li><strong>Pre-made cakes are available for same-day pickup</strong> at most locations in the classic DQ flavor without custom messages. Call ahead to check availability.</li>
    <li><strong>Blizzard Cake flavors may have limited availability</strong> — not every location carries every Blizzard Cake flavor. Call to confirm before ordering.</li>
    <li><strong>Transport time matters</strong> — DQ Cakes can begin to soften within 20–30 minutes outside the freezer. Use a large insulated cooler bag and go directly to your destination.</li>
    <li><strong>Take the cake out 5–10 minutes before serving</strong> — DQ Cake slices cleanest and tastes best at a slight thaw, not straight-from-freezer hard.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The DQ Cake Layer Structure</h2>
  <p>Every DQ Cake, regardless of size, is built in the same layers:</p>
  <ol style="padding-left:1.4rem;line-height:2;">
    <li>Top layer: Whipped topping with decoration and custom message</li>
    <li>Soft serve layer (your chosen flavor, with mix-ins if a Blizzard Cake)</li>
    <li>The crunch center: DQ's signature hot fudge and crunchy middle — the defining layer that sets DQ Cakes apart from generic ice cream cakes</li>
    <li>Second soft serve layer</li>
    <li>Solid base</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The crunch center is what guests most often ask about — it is a proprietary layer of fudge and crispy elements that creates a texture contrast mid-cake. It is the reason DQ Cakes taste different from standard grocery store ice cream cakes.</p>

